  "independent_review": "# Independent read-only review \u2014 2026-11-12\n\nReviewer: /root/independent_review, not an implementation author.\n\nCompared deletion responsibilities at 1ca8ea5 and 3e24e83. The ordinary L serialization/checking branch had a useful retention, fanout and condition-synchronization duty even though the old public writer_join produced only O. The earlier rationale for deletion was withdrawn. Physical line-count constraints have syntax/location replacements; condition implementation has fixed upstream replacements. Initial annotation supervision/readback remain necessary and retained.\n\nRead README.md, docs/examples.md, tools/intake.py, tools/verify.py, tools/run_mixed.py and tests/test_mixed_contract.py in the current candidate. The restored ordinary flow, independent source classification and Liberty condition/sense checks, and event-failing negatives correspond to the documentation. Maintenance readers can locate the real changes and complete diffs; engineers can locate inputs, commands and acceptance criteria.\n\nFound the untouched addf carry === condition boundary. The primary agent reproduced it on the pinned tool: conversion preserves the record, SDF reports COND not supported, carry slots remain at 1 ns, and CO arrives at 11000/21000 ps for A at 10000/20000 ps. Reviewed the amended input contract, scope and validation. They distinguish source preservation from successful timed binding without weakening the original expression or dropping the record. No remaining correctness blocker in the reviewed scope.\n\nIHP review located the retained canonical source identity and unchanged-model compatibility contracts, but no authenticated before/after revision plus SDF for the reported simple-path update. GF180 controls are correctly labeled separately. IHP_REVIEW.json identifies the inspected records. A Docker read attempt was interrupted before providing further evidence; no IHP execution is claimed.\n\nThe independent review did not rerun regressions. Final 14 source tests, 36 annotation controls, nine mixed events/three dynamic negatives and 15 upstream regressions, plus the carry diagnostic probe, were executed and recorded by the primary agent. Local document verification checked 117 links, 37 excerpts, 159 source/generated path locations, all 11 case input records and complete diffs.\n",
  "candidate_manifest_scope": "All distributed files except this manifest. Executed implementation, tests, inputs and references unchanged since the final combined run; prose finalized after review.",
